{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans","id":516156,"title":"Slasher made prometheans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-16T07:05:46-07:00","id":516156,"title":"Slasher made prometheans?","content":"So between a discussion in the general section, the fact that human creators will be much more common in 2d edition, and the movie May, I had a thought: If serial murder can create a promethean, then slashers, who are by definition serial killers, are a solid candidate for a promethean's demiurge.<br /> <br /> So the simple way to do it, of course, is to give a promethean, probably of the frankenstein or galateid lineage, a particularly traumatic backstory.<br /> <br /> On the more ambitious level, one can always come up with a new lineage. <br /> <br /> So has anyone come up with what a promethean made by such a twisted soul might be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T07:19:04-07:00","id":516178,"title":"","content":"Well, the kind of Promethean a Slasher might produce really depends on how they go about it, and possibly their own personality. A slasher who lures his marks with guile and charm would probably produce a Promethean with a sanguine humor, while one who kidnaps people and forces them to play Russian Roulette with them for their lives might produce on with Choleric and Phlegmatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T15:42:51-07:00","id":516512,"title":"","content":"Obviously, the Demiurge's presence and involvement in the Prommie's life is going to play a huge part, and I think the slasher's motivations will as well. A slasher who is trying to build a perfect mate, for example, will possibly come up with a Galateid-like creature; as he searches for parts that meet an aesthetic ideal. Or, he might be driven by the rejection of a previously idealized mate, or even using their their body, and end up with a Wretched from all the bile he's saved up.<br /> <br /> Problem is, the slasher won't get what he wants. In a matter of days, this supreme predator will come to realize all the flaws in his work, and serial killers are nothing if not exacting. He might try to kill the Created and start again, or he might try to make the most of the situation and train the creature to be a lure for new prospects. All of this will be formative for the Promethean. I think Abigail from <i>Hannibal</i> would be an instructive character to look at. One thing I don't think will happen is the slasher letting the Promethean go out on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T16:55:54-07:00","id":516562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=516512#post516512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I don't think will happen is the slasher letting the Promethean go out on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I wouldn't be surprised if a Slasher decided to unleash an angry Promethean on an unsuspecting community and just watch the carnage unfold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T23:07:17-07:00","id":516769,"title":"","content":"True, a slasher setting a promethean to go on his or her merry way doesn't sound to likely.<br /> <br /> That being said, when it comes to physical power, the edge will usually be with the promethean. <br /> <br /> But a promethean killing their demiurge is hardly inconceivable, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T02:25:47-07:00","id":516898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=516562#post516562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I wouldn't be surprised if a Slasher decided to unleash an angry Promethean on an unsuspecting community and just watch the carnage unfold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think slashers tend to make things more personal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T08:01:12-07:00","id":517017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=516898#post516898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think slashers tend to make things more personal...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of true, but a guy can have more than one project going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T06:00:39-07:00","id":517890,"title":"","content":"Looking at it through the Ripper Undertakings...<br /> <br /> Avenger: I can't see an Avenger making a Promethean, even as a way of punishing their victims. The only way I could see it working was as a &quot;someone must carry on my work&quot; thing for an Avenger who thinks the end is drawing nigh - in this case, I'd expect to see something like the Wretched emerge from the process.<br /> <br /> Brute: Brutes can't assemble sentences, let alone bodies - only the hands-on manipulation of a Qashmal would let them do it. Unless you had a Brute assembling parts of victims through mindless instinct, and a freak Fortean phenomenon animate it as an Extemporae.<br /> <br /> Charmer: Again, I can't see a Charmer doing it. People are disposable tools - if you want one, you go get one, you don't go the trouble of putting one together. Unless someone's become the subject of the Obsessive Frailty and dies before the game can be complete, then the Charmer might try to &quot;fix&quot; them so they game can be played out - in that case, I'd expect a Tammuz (built for a purpose they're expected to &quot;naturally&quot; fulfil.<br /> <br /> Freak: Now we're getting somewhere. A Freak trying to make a companion is a perfect match for a Galateid: their origin is suited, their Disquiet makes people feel judged on their looks, their Wasteland makes territory feel off kilter and easy to get lost in (and the Freak has a built-in Talent for getting round that problem), and their Torment can make them stalkers - it's a scarily good match. A place where a Freak has made a Muse is <i>not</i> a good place to find yourself.<br /> <br /> Genius: A Genius might also have a &quot;someone must continue my work vibe,&quot; though in their case I'd expect an Osirian (or maybe an Unfleshed living deathtrap). They might also want a hunting partner or flunky (which could also be an Osirian, or maybe a Tammuz) - or tiring of a world where no one understands their brilliance, they may want to make a mind that can keep up with them (Osirian, or maybe Galateid or Unfleshed). A Genius is probably the Undertaking with the most potential reasons for making a Promethean.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:31:38-07:00","id":518200,"title":"","content":"I don't know, an Avenger might think he can bring the dear lost loved one back, if he just get's the right parts to fix the body... or makes a new, perfect body for his lost loved one's soul. The bastard who killed him isn't using his eyes... You know, that guy who got taken in for assault the other day but got off claims to be a mormon, and they don't even drink tea, so he's probably got a good liver and some kidneys I could use... That punk who broke my windows last night runs track, probably a good heart.<br /> <br /> See what I mean? Hell, getting known for organ theft might even be what turns him into a Legend-he's a madman called the body thief, stealing parts from his victims so he can make a new body for his dead son. But, he can never seem to do it right, so he has to keep doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 05-18-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T08:31:42-07:00","id":519618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=518200#post518200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See what I mean? Hell, getting known for organ theft might even be what turns him into a Legend-he's a madman called the body thief, stealing parts from his victims so he can make a new body for his dead son. But, he can never seem to do it right, so he has to keep doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting idea. I don't really see slashers pursuing a goal whose success would make their reason to kill irrelevant though - I know he always fails in your idea, but he doesn't mean to, and I'm inclined to think an Avenger deep down prefers their loved one to be dead to justify more killing. Though he might self-sabotage his schemes to create a body for that reason, but his obsession still be strong enough that the Fire answers and creates a Promethean almost in spite of the demiurge.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T14:53:12-07:00","id":520039,"title":"","content":"It says right in the book that there are plenty of avengers who put away their knives and try to become productive members of society again. So the idea of an Avenger Specifically pursuing a goal that would ultimately render his need to kill moot kinda fits.<br /> <br /> Besides, after the third or fourth time, when he starts doing truly heinous things to get the right parts, starts getting into the serial killer mold, with the ritualistic behavior and the one specific type of prefered victim(say, healthy males between the ages of 13-16 with similar body types to his son) the stories are gonna start talking about him, and why, he might even forget who he's trying to bring back. He doesn't remember why he's doing it, just that he has to... He has to make these monsters, as he's been trapped in the Story.<br /> <br /> And anyway, I figure he'd make it through at least one attempt, maybe one wit his son's original body, before he becomes a full out slasher and not just a normal serial killer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T18:26:26-07:00","id":520281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=520039#post520039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, after the third or fourth time, when he starts doing truly heinous things to get the right parts, starts getting into the serial killer mold, with the ritualistic behavior and the one specific type of prefered victim(say, healthy males between the ages of 13-16 with similar body types to his son) the stories are gonna start talking about him, and why, he might even forget who he's trying to bring back. He doesn't remember why he's doing it, just that he has to... He has to make these monsters, as he's been trapped in the Story.</div> </div> </div> </div> At the very least, it might make a heck of a personal motivation(as opposed to the general motivation of &quot;become a people&quot;).<br /> <br /> &quot;Dad, listen to me. This isn't right. It's sick, and it's wrong, and it isn't going to bring Tyler back. Dad, you need help. Please, just let me help you! Put down the knife, step away from the kid, and we can talk... please?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T23:55:04-07:00","id":526435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=517890#post517890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at it through the Ripper Undertakings...<br /> <br /> Avenger: I can't see an Avenger making a Promethean, even as a way of punishing their victims. The only way I could see it working was as a &quot;someone must carry on my work&quot; thing for an Avenger who thinks the end is drawing nigh - in this case, I'd expect to see something like the Wretched emerge from the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Rater 202. Avengers are usually motivated by loss.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=517890#post517890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brute: Brutes can't assemble sentences, let alone bodies - only the hands-on manipulation of a Qashmal would let them do it. Unless you had a Brute assembling parts of victims through mindless instinct, and a freak Fortean phenomenon animate it as an Extemporae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever hear of the Batman villain called Humpty Dumpty? Mentally challenged guy obsessed with taking things that didn't work right apart so he could fix them. Eventually, he came to the conclusion that his grandmother was so abusive because something inside her was &quot;broken&quot;...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=517890#post517890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charmer: Again, I can't see a Charmer doing it. People are disposable tools - if you want one, you go get one, you don't go the trouble of putting one together. Unless someone's become the subject of the Obsessive Frailty and dies before the game can be complete, then the Charmer might try to &quot;fix&quot; them so they game can be played out - in that case, I'd expect a Tammuz (built for a purpose they're expected to &quot;naturally&quot; fulfil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charmers progress to Psychos, right? Two words: Norman. Bates.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=517890#post517890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freak: Now we're getting somewhere. A Freak trying to make a companion is a perfect match for a Galateid: their origin is suited, their Disquiet makes people feel judged on their looks, their Wasteland makes territory feel off kilter and easy to get lost in (and the Freak has a built-in Talent for getting round that problem), and their Torment can make them stalkers - it's a scarily good match. A place where a Freak has made a Muse is <i>not</i> a good place to find yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=517890#post517890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius: A Genius might also have a &quot;someone must continue my work vibe,&quot; though in their case I'd expect an Osirian (or maybe an Unfleshed living deathtrap). They might also want a hunting partner or flunky (which could also be an Osirian, or maybe a Tammuz) - or tiring of a world where no one understands their brilliance, they may want to make a mind that can keep up with them (Osirian, or maybe Galateid or Unfleshed). A Genius is probably the Undertaking with the most potential reasons for making a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard not to see Victor as a &quot;Genius&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 05-29-2015, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:40:11-07:00","id":532687,"title":"","content":"Also, supernaturals can BE Slashers...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tumblr_nkni70APVj1s4w2nqo1_540\" target=\"_blank\">http://tumblr_nkni70APVj1s4w2nqo1_540</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 05-31-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:08:44-07:00","id":848739,"title":"","content":"Got sick of the Transhuman thread being top of the page (I know, I was last person to post in it; that just makes me even more so).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=526435#post526435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charmers progress to Psychos, right? Two words: Norman. Bates.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the real reason I'm posting was it occurred to me that we normally consider demiurging a singular activity - but if there's one group of people with the kind of irreducible transgressive obsessions to do it over and over, it would be slashers. Rater202 posted an idea along those lines for a Legend. But what about a Genius who - despairing of finding anyone capable of understanding his brilliance - decides to make minions? Or a Charmer who manufactures an endless string of scapegoats to take the fall for his killings? Or an Avenger who's either not the badass that Undertaking tends to attract, or has been injured beyond continuing to fight, making people to do it for him?<br /> <br /> For that matter, an Avenger might even try to use his dead loved ones as his weapon of choice, rationalising it as allowing them their own vengeance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:09:35-07:00","id":848741,"title":"","content":"(Wrong thread)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T23:52:38-07:00","id":849625,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well, since there's been new unlife in this thread of mine, here's an idea that occurred to me-<br /> <br /> A Slasher identity thief (charmer, genius, whatever) who kills people and takes their place. When he gets bored, he makes a promethean out of his victim, to add to the chaos. <br /> <br /> So the poor promethean would not only be abandoned, but might be in hot water for what they supposedly did before their very birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T04:46:05-07:00","id":850495,"title":"","content":"Here's my question. What kind of Promethean would come out of serial murder? Each of the existing Lineages tend to be a rather iconic archetype.<br /> <br /> Frankenstein - what it says on the tin. Human experimentation for SCIENCE!!! <br /> Osirian - Resurrection Man<br /> Galatea - Stepford Wives / living art / creepy possessed dolls<br /> Tammuz - called golems for a reason. Robo cop would fit here as well.<br /> Ulgan - Wicker people that are sacrificed<br /> Unfleshed - robots not from human bodies<br /> Zeka - nuclear-powered zombie horrors<br /> <br /> Now, what would the purpose behind this be? Serial killers tend to be driven by psychological needs when they kill. The need for control and power primarily. The tropies and actions tied around keeping parts likewise burns with a psychological need to be filled. If we're looking at a sexual killer, then we're talking Galatea. If its an attempt to &quot;save&quot; or reenact someone's death over and over, we're looking at an Osirian. In this respect, killers are no different than non-killer Demiurges. They have an obsession that taps into the Divine Fire. <br /> <br /> Mind you, I think its going to be rare that we get a serial killer that actually can channel the Divine Fire, simply because the act of killing tends to fulfill the psychological need for a time, whereas a Demiurge is going to need to focus on an act of creation as the method of channeling their obsessions. Obsessions. I kind of hope that we get a new look at Demiurges in 2e, because the whole obsession-channels-the-Divine-Fire overlaps waaaaay too much with Mage now. Or maybe we might as well start looking at the Awakened and the Created have as being as interlinked as Vampire and Werewolf seem to be. Magical creators that mess things up, and magical creations that are messed up. <br /> <br /> Anyways! Once we get to the point of creating a Promethean... I'm not really sure how this is really going to be that different from a standard Promethean creation. They're going to be not-quite blank slates that have to deal with their Demiurge with their unbalanced emotions. Demiurges generally aren't immune to the Disquiet of their own creation, so we're going to have creepy obsession actions by both killer and non-killers. The Promethean might pick up some unsavory habits, but I don't think that it will adversely affect the Pilgrimage, which should become milestones to understand these urges and habits. But... I really don't know how else this would have an effect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=849625#post849625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So the poor promethean would not only be abandoned, but might be in hot water for what they supposedly did before their very birth.</div> </div> </div> </div> And what would that be? Go missing? Be kidnapped? Have amnesia about their previous lives? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T11:39:41-07:00","id":850713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/516156-slasher-made-prometheans?p=850495#post850495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what would that be? Go missing? Be kidnapped? Have amnesia about their previous lives?</div> </div> </div> </div>Guilt by association fits really well with Promethean's existing Torment and Disquiet themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T09:36:41-07:00","id":851188,"title":"","content":"Not really. Torment is about the unbalanced mentality the <i>Promethean </i>has, not how others see the Created. As for Promethean Disquiets? Galatea make people feel ashamed or doubt their self-worth. Osirans drive people into despair. The Tammuz Disquiet makes people treat the Golems like their namesake - a machine to use and abuse. The Ulgan enforcing paranoia. That's four out of five Lineages where it makes absolutely no sense. Now, I suppose you could argue that the Frankenstein, who inspires fear and disgust twoards the Lineage members, would do it, but you can't paint the entire gameline with one Lineage's Disquiet effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T10:10:34-07:00","id":851206,"title":"","content":"Your mentality and how others express how they see you is connected. Psych 101...but again, guilt by association. It's perfectly thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}